<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Song Dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Northern Song, Southern Song, Song</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Song Dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> from 960 to 1279, first from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaifeng">Kaifeng</a> in the north and then, after the Jin conquest of the north, from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hangzhou">Hangzhou</a> in the south. It saw remarkable economic growth, urbanisation, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paper-money">paper money</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gunpowder">gunpowder</a> weapons, along with a civil service recruited by examination. It was conquered by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>, who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/song-dynasty.jpg" alt="Song Dynasty" width="320" height="315" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mozzan; derivative work by Kanguole · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:China_-_Song_Dynasty-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
